    "body": "<!-- relay-run-log -->\n**Relay run log** — issue #174\n\n- 2026-09-17 06:56Z — Relay picked up this issue for a BB worker run.\n- 2026-09-17 07:28Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #422 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed successfully. **Branch:** `bb/relay-174-operations-03-08-configure-the-single-thr_7dnkx3mixz` ## Summary Implements issue #174: the single-domain Caddy reverse proxy and the host network boundary. - `deploy/Caddyfile` — automatic TLS/HTTP2, compression, HSTS (`max-age=31536000`, without `includeSubDomains`/`preload`), JSON access log to stderr, `reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080`, and two mutually exclusive `request_body` matchers (`POST /api/files` up to 2GB, everything else capped at 16MB). - `deploy/nftables.conf` — host firewall opening only 22/80/443, with loopback/established traffic allowed and everything else dropped. - `deploy/docker-compose.yml` — PostgreSQL and MinIO, each with host ports explicitly bound to `127.0.0.1`. - `backend/services/semprec-api/src/serve.ts` and `backend/services/semprec-ai-gateway/src/serve.ts` — both HTTP listeners now bind to `127.0.0.1` explicitly in code, not just by relying on the firewall. - `deploy/README.md` and a `README.md` pointer document how these pieces fit together and what's out of scope (no proxy auth/rate-limit/IP-filter/subdomains, no provisioning — later issues in the `operations` batch). Both `backend/pnpm run verify` (lint, format, build, unit, pi-import-paths, migration numbering, write-safety, boundaries, integration 1180/1180, e2e 5/5) and `web/pnpm run verify` (lint, format, build, unit 187/187) pass. 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code) Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-17 07:34Z — Relay BB run is blocked and needs manual follow-up — it will not be retried automatically. Reason: could not request a re-run for code-review check \"code-review\": GitHub API /actions/workflows/code-review.yml/dispatches failed (403): {\"message\":\"Resource no